## DIRECTORY STRUCTURE

```
src/
├── core/
│   ├── types/
│   │   └── index.ts          # All TypeScript interfaces and enums
│   ├── store/
│   │   ├── useAppStore.ts    # App navigation, active role, active scene
│   │   └── usePillboxStore.ts # Pillbox simulation state
│   ├── mocks/
│   │   └── data.ts           # All mock data (patient, meds, history)
│   └── services/
│       └── simulationService.ts  # Business logic (take detection, alerts)
├── scenes/
│   ├── Hub.tsx               # Main landing scene (role selector)
│   ├── PillDispenser3D.tsx   # React Three Fiber 3D scene
│   └── shared/
│       └── Particles.tsx     # Background particle effect
├── components/
│   ├── roles/
│   │   ├── PatientView.tsx   # Patient scenario UI
│   │   ├── CarerView.tsx     # Carer scenario UI
│   │   ├── PharmacistView.tsx # Pharmacist scenario UI
│   │   └── DoctorView.tsx    # Doctor scenario UI
│   └── ui/
│       ├── Panel.tsx         # Reusable glass-panel card
│       ├── AlertBanner.tsx   # Notification / alert component
│       ├── Timeline.tsx      # Medication history timeline
│       ├── Header.tsx        # Top navigation bar
│       ├── RoleCard.tsx      # Role selection card
│       └── StatusBadge.tsx   # Compartment status badge
├── hooks/
│   ├── useSimulation.ts      # Simulation tick logic
│   └── useAudio.ts           # Howler.js audio management
├── App.tsx                   # Root component, scene routing
├── main.tsx                  # Entry point
└── index.css                 # Tailwind base + custom CSS vars
```

---

## NAMING CONVENTIONS

### Files
- React components: PascalCase.tsx (e.g., PatientView.tsx)
- Hooks: camelCase with "use" prefix (e.g., useSimulation.ts)
- Stores: camelCase with "use" prefix (e.g., usePillboxStore.ts)
- Types/Interfaces: PascalCase (e.g., Compartment, MedicationStatus)
- Constants: UPPER_SNAKE_CASE (e.g., COMPARTMENT_SLOTS)
- Mock data: camelCase (e.g., mockPatient, mockHistory)

### Code Conventions
- All interfaces prefixed with "I" ONLY for service/API contracts
- Enums use PascalCase with string values (e.g., CompartmentState.TAKEN = 'taken')
- Zustand stores export a single hook (e.g., export const useAppStore = ...)
- Components must be typed with React.FC<Props> or typed function
- No "any" types — use proper TypeScript typing throughout
- Framer motion variants extracted to constants above component

---

## COMPONENT RULES

### 3D Components (R3F)
- All R3F mesh components must be in src/scenes/
- Use useRef for Three.js object references
- Use useFrame ONLY for continuous animations
- Avoid heavy computations in useFrame — use useMemo for geometries
- All 3D assets use JSX mesh primitives (no external .glb files in POC)

### UI Components
- All components must accept className?: string for extension
- Use Framer Motion for all enter/exit animations
- Minimum touch target: 44px (accessibility for elderly users)
- All interactive elements must have hover AND focus styles
- Use semantic HTML (button, nav, header, main, section)

### State Updates
- Never mutate Zustand state directly — use set() action functions
- Business logic belongs in services/, not in components
- Components only call store actions, never compute derived state inline

